SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: the first section of a constant rounding's walk is not taken
where it is narrower than 5e-4 of the radius (a section by a vanishing
end); the next place along the spine is tried, and such a section is the
start only where no place has another (mitcad#2140, GitHub
mitcad/Mitcad#517).

The case: a Y tube, a circle of radius 10 swept along a line of 25 and a
tangent quarter arc of radius 30, mirrored and joined. The arms (two tori)
meet along a crease, two edges over the crotch's top, whose angle fades to
nothing at both ends where the arms leave the trunk tangentially. The
crease is rounded with 6, 6.5 and 7, but from 8 on the stripe fails with
no piece. The walk's trace (patch 2141): StartSol tries the first place,
0.19 % of the first edge from its start (w 0.058, 0.06 from the vanishing
vertex). At 7 no section is found there, the walk starts at the next place
(w 6.27), walks back into the vanishing end and on over both edges. At 8
the section there is found, its contacts 5e-5 apart, the faces' normals
within 1e-5 rad: the walk back towards the vertex stops after 0.0009 and
ComputeData gives it up as dragging ("If it drags without control,
quit"), and the stripe fails. With the arms' seams turned away from the
crotch the same happens at 6.

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol (of a stripe): a first section found for a
  constant rounding whose contacts are less than 5e-4 of the radius apart
  (the width at which ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing, patch 0771, takes a walk
  into a vanishing end for that end) is not taken; the next place is
  tried. The first such section is taken only where no place along the
  spine gives another, its faces set again where a later place was on
  another edge. Elsewhere nothing changes.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2142.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -1294,6 +1294,11 @@
                   Spine->LastParameter(nbed),
                   Precision::Confusion());
   TopAbs_State Pos1 = TopAbs_UNKNOWN, Pos2 = TopAbs_UNKNOWN;
+  // The first section found narrower than a vanishing end (below).
+  bool     aNarrowFound = false;
+  gp_Pnt2d aNarrowP1, aNarrowP2;
+  double   aNarrowW    = 0.;
+  int      aNarrowEdge = 0;
   for (nbessai = 0; nbessai <= nbessaimax; nbessai++)
   {
     double t  = nbessai * unsurnbessaimax;
@@ -1398,10 +1403,52 @@
     {
       P1.SetCoord(SolDep(1), SolDep(2));
       P2.SetCoord(SolDep(3), SolDep(4));
+      // (A section narrower than 5e-4 of the radius, as where
+      // ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing takes a walk into a vanishing end for that
+      // end, is no start: the walk from it towards the end stalls at once and
+      // drags, mitcad#2140. The next place is tried; it starts there only
+      // where no other place has a section.)
+      if (!aKnifeSpine.IsNull() && aKnifeSpine->IsConstant(iedge)
+          && HS1->Value(SolDep(1), SolDep(2)).Distance(HS2->Value(SolDep(3), SolDep(4)))
+               < 5.e-4 * aKnifeSpine->Radius(iedge))
+      {
+        if (!aNarrowFound)
+        {
+          aNarrowFound = true;
+          aNarrowP1    = P1;
+          aNarrowP2    = P2;
+          aNarrowW     = w;
+          aNarrowEdge  = iedge;
+        }
+        if (ChFi3d_TracingWalkOnSpine())
+        {
+          std::fprintf(stderr, "fillet walk: the section at w %.9g is narrower than a vanishing end: no start\n", w);
+        }
+        continue;
+      }
       First = w;
       return;
     }
   }
+  if (aNarrowFound)
+  {
+    // (No place but narrow ones: the first of them, as before.)
+    if (aNarrowEdge != iedge)
+    {
+      ConexFaces(Spine, aNarrowEdge, HS1, HS2);
+      I1->Initialize((const occ::handle<Adaptor3d_Surface>&)HS1);
+      const occ::handle<Adaptor3d_Surface>& aHSon2 = HS2; // to avoid ambiguity
+      I2->Initialize(aHSon2);
+    }
+    P1    = aNarrowP1;
+    P2    = aNarrowP2;
+    First = aNarrowW;
+    if (ChFi3d_TracingWalkOnSpine())
+    {
+      std::fprintf(stderr, "fillet walk: only narrow sections: the start at w %.9g\n", aNarrowW);
+    }
+    return;
+  }
   // No solution was found for the faces adjacent to the trajectory.
   // Now one tries the neighbor faces.
   iedge = 0;
